# Gradle
.gradle/
build/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
# IDE (Eclipse/VSCode-Java) compile output inside each module — never committed.
# Eclipse/redhat.java compile the tree into `<module>/bin/{main,test}` beside Gradle's `build/`.
# Matched at ANY depth on purpose: the previous pattern was `java/*/bin/`, which stopped covering
# anything the moment modules moved out of `java/`, and a `git add -A` then committed 1,127 .class
# files. Anchored on `bin/main` and `bin/test` rather than a bare `bin/` so that Cargo's own
# `tracker/src/bin/` convention — which holds real source — keeps working.
**/bin/main/
**/bin/test/
.vscode/
.eclipse/
.classpath
.project
.settings/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Nodera runtime artifacts (anchored to repo root — an unanchored `nodera/` would also
# match the `dev/nodera/` source package in every module and silently hide new source files).
/nodera/
/divergences/
/world-store/

# NOTE: third-party architecture-study clones are NOT ignored. They live in
# docs/minecraft/upstream/ as pinned submodules (see .gitmodules) so a study document and
# the upstream commit it describes cannot drift apart. The two rules that used to sit here
# pointed at docs/Context/, a directory deleted in the 2026-07-25 docs reorg.

# jqwik property-test database (runtime artifact)
.jqwik-database

# Local NeoForge dedicated-server install (created by scripts/setup-server.sh):
# downloaded NeoForge libraries, world saves, logs, the copied mod jar — never committed.
/run/

# Stray Minecraft/NeoForge runtime logs if a server is ever launched from the repo root.
/logs/
/latest.log
/debug.log
/crash-reports/
hs_err_pid*.log

# Local API-token / env files — MUST never be committed (contain ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN etc.)
claude_code_zai_env.sh
/a
*.env
.env

# Cargo build output. Matched at ANY depth on purpose: this pattern used to be `/target/`, which
# was anchored at the repository root while the workspace actually lived under `rust/`. It matched
# nothing, and a `git add -A` then committed 1.4 GB of `rust/target` debug binaries and incremental
# dep-graphs — 99% of the repository — which had to be removed by rewriting history. The workspace
# has since moved to the root and `app/` keeps a second one, so no pattern that names a directory
# can be trusted to survive the next move. Nothing tracked has a `target` path component.
target/

# Local agent/plugin settings (per-machine, not project config).
/.claude/

# NeoForge dev runs (MDG runClient/runServer/runClientJoin game dirs)
endpoints/neoforge-mod/run/
endpoints/neoforge-mod/run-join/
endpoints/neoforge-mod/run-join2/
endpoints/neoforge-mod/run-join3/
endpoints/neoforge-mod/run-host/

# Telemetry deployment (docker/telemetry/) — secrets, TLS material, and collected data never land
# in git. The .example files and the configuration ARE committed; what they point at is not.
docker/telemetry/.env
docker/telemetry/edge/certs/*
!docker/telemetry/edge/certs/.gitkeep
telemetry-spool/

# Kotlin build-daemon crash logs from build-logic (per-machine, never useful in git).
library/java/build-logic/.kotlin/

# The built website. `scripts/build-site.sh` writes web/dist and docker/web/Dockerfile rebuilds it
# inside the image, so a committed copy would be a second answer to "what is the site" that nothing
# ever checks against the first. The sources in web/ are committed; what a build makes of them is
# not.
web/dist/
# The intermediate server bundle the prerenderer imports, and the data the site reads out of this
# repository at build time — the release manifest, the service list, the roadmap and limitation
# counts, the launcher's palette, the mirrored documents. All of it is derived, all of it is
# regenerated by `bun run --cwd web prebuild`, and a committed copy would be a second answer to
# "what does the repository say" that nothing ever checks against the first.
web/.ssr/
web/src/generated/*.json

# Every JavaScript dependency directory, at every depth. The three frontend packages
# (library/ts/nodera-ui, app/ui, web) are one bun workspace and its install HOISTS to the repository
# root, so `web/node_modules` and `app/ui/node_modules` stopped being the only two that can appear —
# bun still leaves a per-package directory behind whenever a version cannot hoist. A rule naming the
# directories that happened to exist when it was written is the same silent staleness
# `check-layout-drift.sh` exists to catch, so this one names the shape instead.
node_modules/

# `bun.lock` is TRACKED, deliberately, and there is exactly one of it — at the repository root,
# because the workspace resolves as a unit. `app/.gitignore` used to ignore `/ui/bun.lock`, which
# meant `scripts/build-app-ui.sh`'s `bun install --frozen-lockfile` had never had a lockfile to be
# frozen against: the whole dependency graph re-resolved on every CI run and nobody reviewed the
# change. That is the argument `app/.gitignore` already makes at length for tracking `app/Cargo.lock`.
#
# A conflict in it is always resolved by re-running `bun install` and committing the result, never
# by editing it by hand.
!bun.lock

# Python bytecode (the Spark jobs are sources, never build output).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Service node identities. A locally started tracker or rendezvous writes its Ed25519 secret key
# next to the working directory it was launched from, so these appear wherever a service was run.
# They are private keys: committing one hands over the identity of that node permanently.
*-identity.bin

# Signing key material. A safety net, not a workflow: the Android release keystore lives outside
# this repository and reaches CI as a secret. This exists because the cost of one accidental
# `git add -A` is unbounded — an Android signing key that leaks cannot be rotated, since Android
# identifies an app by its certificate and every existing install would refuse an update signed by
# a new one.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx

# Blender's rolling backup of a saved .blend — it writes one on every save, next to the file it
# backs up. `branding/logo.blend` IS committed; a second copy of it that changes on every render is
# not, and at 2.8 MB it is bigger than the file it duplicates.
*.blend1
